+  Override rows key on the record name, so a name shared by two schools blanks both. Check for
+  duplicate names before writing a blanking row. 16 names in the corpus are carried by more
+  than one record, and "Evolution Jiu Jitsu" above is one of them.
+
+  AND CHECK THE REMOVED INDEX, NOT ONLY THE OVERRIDE FILES. Both rendering surfaces drop a
+  record whose name appears in its region's tjjm-removed-index row, so renaming a record can
+  silently ADD it back to a region page and move that region's count. Suppression and blanking
+  are different mechanisms; a name can be caught by either, or by both.
